The function already does very little, so the realistic gain is small. The rewrite reads the `profile` member once into a local, so the compiler doesn't reload it for the bounds check and the field access. It also checks the common valid case first, so that path has a single branch. The returned value is the same for every input.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumSubFields(void) const
{
    const auto* const p = profile;
    if (p != NULL)
    {
        const auto idx = profileIndex;
        if (idx < p->numFields)
            return p->fields[idx].numSubFields;
    }
    return 0;
}
```